description:
FILED s536f (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-08) from the #4644 tie-count probes (scratch/s536f/p/m3e.pl in the s536f worktree).  PRE-EXISTING: main c8886b61 answers the same.

REPRODUCER (probed vs perl 5.40.3):

    my $c = 0; sub f { $c++; 1 }
    my %h = (v => 1); ($h{v} += f())++; print "1 $h{v} $c\n";
    my $x = 1; ($x += f())++; print "2 $x $c\n";
    my @a = (1); ++($a[0] += f()); print "3 $a[0] $c\n";
    ($h{w} = f())--; print "4 $h{w} $c\n";

perl: `1 3 1` / `2 3 2` / `3 3 3` / `4 0 4`.   PCL: `1 5 3` / `2 5 6` / `3 4 8` / `4 0 11`.

MECHANISM (read, not fixed): the emission is `(p-post++ (p-incf (p-gethash-box %h "v") (pl-f)))`; p-post++'s general arm (cl/pcl-runtime.lisp, the `t` arm) binds `(%p-incdec-old REAL-PLACE)` and then emits REAL-PLACE again inside `%p-incdec-store-form` and `%p-read-operand` -- a non-symbol, non-accessor operand form (an assignment, a compound assignment) is EVALUATED once per mention.  The fix shape: when REAL-PLACE is not a symbol / accessor place, bind it ONCE to a temp (it answers the lvalue BOX since s536f #4644 -- p-incf / p-setf of a box place answer the box) and increment that box; the same for p-pre++ / p-post-- / p-pre--.  With a TIED element the extra evaluations show as extra FETCH / STORE calls (`($t{v} += 1)++`: perl fetch 2 / store 2, PCL 4 / 4 -- the row in Pl/t/elem-assign-lvalue-01.t #4644 keeps that count out of its assertion for this task).
BAR: the reproducer as a guard row; the ++ / -- Pl/t files.
